In <1993Dec19.224512.4003@vlsi.polymtl.ca>, Christian Laforte writes:
> I've been watching this newsgroup for several weeks, and I heard several times
> of a variant of our favorite game named "NetHack--".
> 
> Could someone finally tell us poor ignorants WHERE WE CAN FIND IT!?!?!?!
> 
> Unix sources or IBM executables would be perfect.

Look on wuarchive.wustl.edu:/pub/MSDOS_UPLOADS/games/nh-- for the
NetHack-- souce code, which can be compiled for OS/2, DOS (eeew), Atari
ST, Amiga, VMS, UNIX, Mac, etc just like normal NetHack.

You should really say what OS you're running, since PCs can run DOS (the
worst and most popular choice), OS/2, several kinds of UNIX including
NeXTstep, Solaris, and Linux, etc...

> And finally, what are the major differences between this version and the
> original nethack?

Not much really.  Over a hundred new monsters, some new items, some new
artifacts.  If anyone else wants to take over development or
maintainance, let me know, I've redirected my energies to other
places...

